CloudBurrow patch 14 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1127); needs patch 0013.

The bug: JSON_OBJECT, JSON_ARRAY, JSON_SET, JSON_ARRAY_APPEND and
JSON_ARRAY_INSERT use TO_JSON's encoding for their values (GoogleSQL's
JSON encodings table), but wrote each value with its own ToJSON: a BOOL
read from a table was 1, a DATE, DATETIME, TIME or TIMESTAMP was unquoted
(not JSON), and JSON_SET of a DATE failed "strconv.ParseFloat".

The patch has the formatter wrap each value argument whose type is not
STRING, INT64, FLOAT64 or JSON in the typed TO_JSON of patch 0013
(internal/json_value_args.go), so the function is given JSON it embeds as
it is. An ARRAY given to JSON_ARRAY_APPEND or JSON_ARRAY_INSERT is left as
before, since those add its elements one by one. json_value_args_test.go
fails without the patch.

